Lobium — WebGL runtime capability safety.

Never advertise a configured WebGL capability which the active GL backend cannot execute. Numeric
MAX_* values are clamped to the backend and configured extension lists are intersected with extensions
the backend can actually enable. This prevents heavy 3D engines from selecting 16K resources or an
unsupported extension on an 8K SwiftShader host, while retaining exact configured values on capable
hardware. Requires core/config-channel.patch and fingerprint/host-gpu-profile.patch.

